The '''Dalmar Period''' ([[Burawi language|Burawi]]: ''Xilligii Dalmar'') was the second major era of the [[Kingdom of Ufyen]], spanning approximately 400 to 150 BCE. It encompasses two dynasties — the '''Dalmar Dynasty''' and its successor the '''Barre Dynasty''' — and is characterised by a shift in Ufyen strategy from direct territorial control to the management of trade chokepoints, and by the prolonged economic rivalry with the coastal city-states known as the [[Ancient Southwestern Kaftia#The tariff wars|Tariff Wars]].

